 ◆ self-host                                                                                                      v1.0.0

  Your own web address

  ╭─────────────╮      ╭────────────╮      ╭───────────────╮
  │ anyone with │──────│ Cloudflare │──────│ this computer │
  │ the address │      │ login page │      │ no open port  │
  ╰─────────────╯      ╰─────┬──────╯      ╰───────────────╯
                       login first ✓

  Your own web address, like movies.example.com, opens your chosen Apps from anywhere through
  Cloudflare Tunnel, without opening any port on your router. A login page stands in front, so
  only people you allow get in. Choose Apps after they are installed; nothing goes public without
  a separate yes.

  Before you begin
  Add your main domain to Cloudflare and wait until it is active. At one.dash.cloudflare.com
  choose a team name, the Zero Trust Free plan (50 users), and a payment method that is not
  charged. Use the main domain, not a sub-domain: deeper names need a paid certificate.

  Create one private API token
  In Cloudflare: My Profile > API Tokens > Create Token > Create Custom Token. Account
  permissions: Cloudflare Tunnel: Edit; Access: Apps and Policies: Edit; Access: Organizations,
  Identity Providers, and Groups: Edit. Zone permissions: DNS: Edit; Zone: Read. Limit resources
  to your one account and one zone. Enter the token privately; only the tunnel run token is saved.
  Changes and removal ask for the API token again.

